3. What you may not do
You may not, and may not let anyone else:
  a. copy, sell, rent, lease, lend, sublicense or redistribute the Software,
     in whole or in part, or put it on a website, share or download service;
  b. reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, or try to
     obtain its source code, except where the law allows this despite this
     clause;
  c. modify the Software or make works based on it, except for the
     configuration files, scripts and integrations the Software expects you to
     edit, and the use of its documented API;
  d. remove or change any copyright, licence or trademark notice;
  e. bypass or disable the safety gates, rate-limit protections or licence
     terms of the Software or of any broker or data provider it connects to.

4. Third-party components
The Software includes components written by others (for example Node.js and
